                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "N7Lpy",
                  "name": "Body",
                  "context": "div.column · PortableBody ← content (blockContent), gap 22",
                  "width": 720,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 22,
                  "alignItems": "center",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "ushIp",
                      "name": "Lead",
                      "context": "Lead · first block, 17",
                      "fill": "$a-ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "It took me three years and a handful of embarrassing product demos to realize that the place where my interface felt uncanny wasn't the data layer, the animation library, or even the typography — it was the loading state. The brief, ugly, half-loaded moment between ask and answer.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$af-ui",
                      "fontSize": 17,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "vqvYC",
                      "context": "h2 ← blockContent h2 style, display 30",
                      "fill": "$a-ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Why loaders fail",
                      "lineHeight": 1.15,
                      "fontFamily": "$af-display",
                      "fontSize": 30,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "YZcwr",
                      "context": "p ← blockContent normal block, 17/1.65 $a-ink",
                      "fill": "$a-ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A spinner gets a free pass. It's expected to look generic, because its job is to be invisible — a placeholder for the thing that hasn't happened yet. We rarely critique it. A skeleton doesn't get the same grace. When the placeholder looks more designed than the page it occupies, the user starts waiting for content that already feels like content, and that waiting is where the slowness lives.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$af-ui",
                      "fontSize": 17,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "qFa0w",
                      "context": "h2 ← blockContent h2 style, display 30",
                      "fill": "$a-ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The three dimensions",
                      "lineHeight": 1.15,
                      "fontFamily": "$af-display",
                      "fontSize": 30,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "H3qs7",
                      "context": "p ← blockContent normal block, 17/1.65 $a-ink",
                      "fill": "$a-ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "When we started treating skeletons as a first-class surface in our design system, we gave them three dimensions to think about. The shape — does it communicate what kind of content is coming? The rhythm — does its motion feel like the rest of our product, or like an interruption? And the contract — when real content lands, does it reveal cleanly, or does the transition tell the user to start over?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$af-ui",
                      "fontSize": 17,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "lbRdD",
                      "name": "Quote",
                      "context": "blockquote ← blockContent blockquote style, 3px $a-accent bar",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "padding": [
                        4,
                        32
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "A46hNx",
                          "name": "Quote body",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 12,
                          "padding": [
                            8,
                            0
                          ],
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "rectangle",
                              "cornerRadius": 2,
                              "id": "i8BBi",
                              "name": "bar",
                              "fill": "$a-accent",
                              "width": 3,
                              "height": 0
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "frame",
                              "id": "s43TqS",
                              "name": "Quote text",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "layout": "vertical",
                              "gap": 8,
                              "padding": [
                                16,
                                24
                              ],
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "id": "xtFOu",
                                  "name": "t",
                                  "fill": "$a-ink",
                                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                                  "width": "fill_container",
                                  "content": "A skeleton is a promise your UI makes to the user — break that promise and the page feels exponentially slower.",
                                  "lineHeight": 1.35,
                                  "fontFamily": "$af-display",
                                  "fontSize": 24,
                                  "fontWeight": "normal",
                                  "fontStyle": "italic"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "id": "Y5NDDs",
                                  "name": "a",
                                  "fill": "$a-faint",
                                  "content": "KYLE ROSS · INTERNAL MEMO, 2024",
                                  "fontFamily": "$af-ui",
                                  "fontSize": 13,
                                  "fontWeight": "normal",
                                  "letterSpacing": 0.4
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "jcuAV",
                      "context": "h2 ← blockContent h2 style, display 30",
                      "fill": "$a-ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "What this looks like in code",
                      "lineHeight": 1.15,
                      "fontFamily": "$af-display",
                      "fontSize": 30,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "D5mK7",
                      "context": "p ← blockContent normal block, 17/1.65 $a-ink",
                      "fill": "$a-ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Here is the smallest piece of the system that made the rest of the work possible: a skeleton that knows what it's standing in for. It carries a hint about shape, but the rhythm — the breath — is what makes it feel alive.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$af-ui",
                      "fontSize": 17,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "C2I66",
                      "name": "Code block",
                      "context": "figure.code · CodeBlock ← blockContent code{language, code, filename} · r8, 1px $a-line, bg $a-code-bg · Shiki theme from --a-code-* (portable/media.ts) · pre scrolls horizontally",
                      "clip": true,
                      "width": 720,
                      "fill": "$a-code-bg",
